);"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Annual limit, radiation worker"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono","style":"color: rgb(251, 146, 60);"},"20 mSv"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full mt-1","aria-hidden":"true","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);"},["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full","style":"width: 64.6142%; background: rgb(251, 146, 60);"}]]]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Lowest dose with clear cancer link"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono","style":"color: rgb(251, 146, 60);"},"100 mSv"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full mt-1","aria-hidden":"true","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);"},["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full","style":"width: 73.134%; background: rgb(251, 146, 60);"}]]]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Radiation sickness begins"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"1,000 mSv"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full mt-1","aria-hidden":"true","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);"},["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full","style":"width: 85.323%; background: rgb(248, 113, 113);"}]]]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Fatal without treatment (about half)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"4,500 mSv"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full mt-1","aria-hidden":"true","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);"},["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full","style":"width: 93.285%; background: rgb(248, 113, 113);"}]]]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Highest Chernobyl responder doses"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"16,000 mSv"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full mt-1","aria-hidden":"true","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.15);"},["SPAN",{"class":"block h-1.5 rounded-full","style":"width: 100%; background: rgb(248, 113, 113);"}]]]]],["DIV",{"data-nk-exploration-progress":"dosesSeen","class":"nk-exploration-progress flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-2 rounded-lg border px-2.5 py-1.5","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.333); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5);"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"Try another option"],["PROGRESS",{"value":"0","max":"5","aria-label":"0 of 5 dose examples deliberately compared","class":"flex-1 min-w-[7rem] h-2","style":"accent-color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"}],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"0 of 5 dose examples deliberately compared"]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"Where the science is genuinely unsettled"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"At and above about 100 mSv, excess cancer risk is measurable in survivor studies. Below that, epidemiological studies have limited statistical power because ordinary cancer is common and the possible addition is small. Regulators use the linear no-threshold model as a cautious protection assumption. Evidence at low dose remains uncertain rather than proving either zero risk or a measured effect; be wary of claims that treat either conclusion as settled."]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-lowdose","data-nk-sec":"lowdose","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-lowdose","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.333) rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.333) rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.333) rgb(232, 121, 249); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-lowdose","style":"color: rgb(232, 121, 249); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.267);"},"📉 12. How risky is a small dose? Why one event gets two death tolls"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Everything above 100 mSv on the ladder is measured. Everything below it is modelled — and the model you pick is where the public argument actually lives. Two people can quote the same accident, use the same physics, make no arithmetic error, and differ by a factor of a hundred on the death toll. Here is how."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Pick an exposure"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"One person, one CT of the abdomen. Use the exposure: One person, one CT of the abdomen, 10 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"One person, one CT of the abdomen"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"530,000 Chernobyl recovery workers, 120 mSv each. Use the exposure: 530,000 Chernobyl recovery workers, 120 mSv each, 120 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"530,000 Chernobyl recovery workers, 120 mSv each"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"100,000 aircrew, 3 mSv a year for 20 years. Use the exposure: 100,000 aircrew, 3 mSv a year for 20 years, 60 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"100,000 aircrew, 3 mSv a year for 20 years"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"A city of 1 million, 1 mSv each after a release. Use the exposure: A city of 1 million, 1 mSv each after a release, 1 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(251, 146, 60); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(251, 146, 60);"},"A city of 1 million, 1 mSv each after a release"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"500 million people, 0.05 mSv each. Use the exposure: 500 million people, 0.05 mSv each, 0.05 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"500 million people, 0.05 mSv each"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Everyone on Earth eats a banana a day for a year. Use the exposure: Everyone on Earth eats a banana a day for a year, 0.0365 millisieverts each","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Everyone on Earth eats a banana a day for a year"]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(232, 121, 249, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(232, 121, 249);"},"1 million people × 1 mSv = 1,000 person-sieverts"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-1.5","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"One collective dose. Four ways to turn it into a number of people."],["DIV",{"role":"list","class":"space-y-1"},["DIV",{"role":"listitem","aria-label":"Linear no-threshold: 55 deaths","class":"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-1.5 py-1","style":"background: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.12);"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"LNT (ICRP)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono font-black text-right","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"55 deaths"]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem","aria-label":"Linear, with no low-dose-rate discount: 110 deaths","class":"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-1.5 py-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Linear, no discount"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono font-black text-right","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"110 deaths"]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem","aria-label":"Threshold at 100 mSv: zero","class":"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-1.5 py-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Threshold"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono font-black text-right","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"zero"]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem","aria-label":"Hormesis: no defensible number","class":"flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-1.5 py-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Hormesis"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono font-black text-right","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153);"},"no defensible number"]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-md border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.533); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"Can you use this sum? A planning quantity, not a body count"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Between about 1 and 100 mSv the number is below what epidemiology can resolve, but the individual doses are still large enough to be worth managing. Use it to COMPARE options — shelter against evacuate, scan against no scan — and not as a prediction of identifiable deaths."]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"The emergency-planning case. One millisievert each is small individually and large collectively, and this is exactly the calculation an authority runs to compare sheltering against evacuating. Treat the answer as a planning quantity for comparing OPTIONS, not as a prediction of identifiable deaths."]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Now read one model properly"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"LNT (ICRP). Explain the Linear no-threshold model","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(167, 139, 250); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"LNT (ICRP)"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Linear, no discount. Explain the Linear, with no low-dose-rate discount model","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Linear, no discount"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Threshold. Explain the Threshold at 100 mSv model","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Threshold"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Hormesis. Explain the Hormesis model","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Hormesis"]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.467); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"Linear no-threshold"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-mono mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"5.5% per sievert"],["DIV",{"class":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 mt-2"},["DIV",{},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"WHAT IT CLAIMS"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Risk is proportional to dose all the way down to zero, with no safe threshold. Half the dose, half the risk — never none."]],["DIV",{},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"WHO USES IT"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"ICRP, the US NRC, the EPA, and every national regulator. Every dose limit in this tool comes from it."]],["DIV",{},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153);"},"THE CASE FOR IT"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"It fits the atomic-bomb survivor data well above 100 mSv, it is simple to administer, and it errs in the direction that protects people. The pooled study of over 300,000 nuclear workers exposed slowly across whole careers (INWORKS) finds a dose-response consistent with a straight line rather than with a threshold."]],["DIV",{},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"THE CASE AGAINST IT"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Below about 100 mSv it is an extrapolation, not a measurement. It is routinely applied several orders of magnitude outside the range where anyone has tested it."]]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(34, 211, 238);"},"So why not just go and measure it?"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed mb-1","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"People have tried, and the obstacle is not funding or will — it is arithmetic. About a quarter of everyone dies of cancer anyway, so to see a small addition you need an exposed group and a matched unexposed group big enough that the difference is not noise. Set the dose and read off how many people that takes."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"ld-pow","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Dose to detect"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"20","id":"ld-pow","type":"range","min":"0","max":"30","step":"1","aria-valuetext":"10 mSv","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"20"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"ld-pow","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"10 mSv"]],["DIV",{"class":"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 mt-2"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"People needed in each group"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(34, 211, 238);"},"9.7 million"]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Both groups together"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"19.5 million"]]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Ten times smaller dose, a HUNDRED times the people: the excess enters the sizing squared, so the requirement grows as the inverse square of the dose. At 10 mSv — one CT scan — the answer is already larger than any radiation cohort ever assembled; at 1 mSv it exceeds the population of most countries. Published estimates agree: Brenner and colleagues put the 10 mSv study at roughly 5 million per group under slightly more favourable assumptions."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Slide it to 100 mSv and watch what the calculation says: about a hundred thousand people per group. The atomic-bomb survivor study follows roughly that many — and 100 mSv is exactly where this tool says the excess becomes measurable. That is not a coincidence, and it is the check on this arithmetic: the same formula that says the low-dose question is unanswerable correctly predicts where the answer we DO have came from."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Two-proportion sample size at 5% significance and 80% power, against a 25% baseline lifetime cancer mortality, using the ICRP coefficient. It assumes something even a perfect study could not have: that every person's dose is known exactly and nothing else differs between the groups. The real requirement is larger."]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.6); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"What this section is NOT saying"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Not that low-dose radiation is harmless: no threshold has ever been demonstrated, and the best evidence at low dose RATE — the pooled nuclear-worker cohorts — is consistent with a straight line rather than a floor. Not that the regulators are wrong either: assuming linearity when you cannot measure is the cautious choice, and caution is what a limit is for. What remains genuinely disputed among radiation biologists is the shape of the curve below about 100 mSv, and the honest answer to \"how many will this kill\" at those doses is that the arithmetic gives a number and the world may not. Be equally suspicious of anyone who quotes that number as a body count and of anyone who tells you it is zero."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"This is where the Chernobyl range in section 15 comes from. Apply the model to the most exposed few hundred thousand people and you get a projection of a few thousand; apply the same model to a whole continent receiving doses smaller than the difference between two towns' background, and you get tens of thousands. Neither side fabricated anything. They chose a different population, and the model does not know it is being asked something it cannot answer."]],["ASIDE",{"role":"note","aria-label":"Educational safety notice","class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6); background: rgba(69, 10, 10, 0.35);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Educational model — not emergency or medical instructions"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(254, 202, 202);"},"This personal-dose estimate is educational, not a medical assessment. Ask a qualified clinician, health physicist, or local radon program about a real exposure."],["A",{"href":"https://www.nrc.gov/about-nrc/emerg-preparedness/in-radiological-emerg","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"inline-block mt-1 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold underline","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Official NRC emergency guidance ↗"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Sources · reviewed 2026-08: ",["A",{"href":"https://www.icrp.org/publication.asp?id=ICRP%20Publication%20103","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"ICRP Publication 103 (2007)"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.bmj.com/content/382/bmj-2022-074520","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"INWORKS worker cohort, BMJ 2023"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.unscear.org/unscear/en/publications/2020_2021_2.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"UNSCEAR Fukushima 2020/21"]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-detect","data-nk-sec":"detect","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-detect","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.333) rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.333) rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.333) rgb(45, 212, 191); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-detect","style":"color: rgb(45, 212, 191); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.267);"},"🔬 13. Measure it yourself — and why one short count lies"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Every figure above came out of a detector, and a detector does not measure sieverts. It measures clicks — and radioactive decay is random, so the same source counted twice gives two different answers. Neither is wrong. Take some counts and watch it happen."],["DIV",{"class":"grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2 mb-2"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.333); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"Becquerel (Bq)"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"What the SOURCE does"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"One decay per second, inside the source. It does not depend on you, your detector, or where you stand."]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.333); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(45, 212, 191);"},"Counts per second"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"What the DETECTOR sees"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Always far less. Most photons miss the window entirely, and the tube ignores most of the ones that arrive. Never quote a count rate without saying which instrument, at what distance."]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.333); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"Millisievert (mSv)"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"What YOUR BODY absorbs"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Energy deposited per kilogram of tissue, weighted for how much damage that kind of radiation does. Getting here from counts needs a calibrated instrument and the photon energy."]]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Put something in front of the tube"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Background only. Measure Background only. No source at all.","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Background only"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"One banana. Measure One banana. ≈0.45 g of potassium, so ≈14 Bq of K-40.","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"One banana"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"1 kg salt substitute (KCl). Measure 1 kg salt substitute (KCl). 524 g of potassium at 31.7 Bq/g.","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"1 kg salt substitute (KCl)"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"Cs-137 check source, 37 kBq. Measure Cs-137 check source, 37 kBq. 1 µCi sealed disc, 662 keV gamma in 85.1% of decays.","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(45, 212, 191); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(45, 212, 191);"},"Cs-137 check source, 37 kBq"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Co-60 check source, 37 kBq. Measure Co-60 check source, 37 kBq. 1 µCi, and TWO gammas per decay (1.17 and 1.33 MeV).","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Co-60 check source, 37 kBq"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"1 µCi sealed disc, 662 keV gamma in 85.1% of decays. — 37,000 Bq, giving off about 31,487 gammas a second in all directions."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"nk-cd-dist","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Distance"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"10","id":"nk-cd-dist","type":"range","min":"3","max":"60","step":"1","aria-valuetext":"10 cm","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"10"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"nk-cd-dist","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"10 cm"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Count for"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"5 s. Count for 5 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"5 s"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"10 s. Count for 10 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(45, 212, 191); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(45, 212, 191);"},"10 s"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"30 s. Count for 30 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"30 s"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"1 min. Count for 60 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"1 min"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"5 min. Count for 300 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"5 min"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"10 min. Count for 600 seconds","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"10 min"]],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-2"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-label":"Take a count. Measure Cs-137 check source, 37 kBq for 10 seconds at 10 centimetres, with a matching background count","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"background: rgb(45, 212, 191); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(45, 212, 191);"},"⏱️ Take a count"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-2","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"No counts yet. Each press runs the detector twice: once with the source, once with it removed, for the same length of time. That second run is not optional — you cannot subtract a background you never measured."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-chart-frame rounded-lg overflow-hidden border mt-2","style":"border-color: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.35); height: 170px;"},["CANVAS",{"__playwright_bounding_rect__":"{\"left\":41,\"top\":73469.703125,\"right\":41,\"bottom\":73687.703125}","role":"img","data-a11y-static":"true","aria-describedby":"nk-count-description","aria-label":"Net count rate against distance for Cs-137 check source, 37 kBq. The curve follows the inverse square law: at 10 centimetres the true rate is 1.543 counts per second, and doubling the distance to 20 centimetres quarters it to 0.386.","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;"}]],["P",{"id":"nk-count-description","class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"The curve is the inverse square law, and it is not a property of radiation — it is a property of spheres. The same gammas spread over a surface four times larger when you step twice as far back. Doubling your distance does more than most shielding, costs nothing, and is why the first rule of a radiation area is stand further away."],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 146, 60, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(251, 146, 60);"},"The trap in every cheap counter"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Consumer Geiger counters show a number in µSv/h, which makes them look like dose meters. They are not. The tube counts clicks and the display multiplies by one fixed factor — almost always the one that is correct for caesium-137 at 662 keV. Point the same instrument at a lower-energy source and the reading can be out by a factor of several, in either direction. This is the single most common way a well-meaning measurement ends up wrong on the internet: the instrument is fine, the counting is fine, and the conversion was never valid for what was being measured."]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"End-window GM tube, 6.16 cm² window, intrinsic efficiency 0.8–1.0% and background 25 counts/min — typical of school apparatus at sea level. Counts are drawn from a Poisson distribution, the real statistics of decay. Detection threshold is the Currie critical level for a paired background, 2.33√(2N_b), a 5% chance of crying wolf. Source activities: 37 kBq check sources, potassium at 31.7 Bq per gram of natural K, K-40 emitting its 1461 keV gamma in 10.6% of decays."]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-protect","data-nk-sec":"protect","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-protect","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgb(56, 189, 248); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-protect","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.267);"},"⏱️ 14. Time, distance, shielding — all three levers"],["ASIDE",{"role":"note","aria-label":"Educational safety notice","class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6); background: rgba(69, 10, 10, 0.35);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Educational model — not emergency or medical instructions"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(254, 202, 202);"},"Follow the nuclear-medicine team's written discharge instructions. Never use this calculator to set a real contact time or handle a sealed source."],["A",{"href":"https://www.nrc.gov/about-nrc/emerg-preparedness/in-radiological-emerg","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"inline-block mt-1 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold underline","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Official NRC emergency guidance ↗"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Section 5 covered what stops radiation and section 13 covered distance. There is a third lever, it is free, and it is the one a radiation worker reaches for first: leave sooner. Dose is dose rate accumulated over time. A steady rate is simple multiplication; when a radionuclide is decaying, the rate must be integrated as it falls."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"What are you standing near?"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Someone who has just had a bone scan. Someone who has just had a bone scan, Tc-99m, 0.8 gigabecquerels","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Someone who has just had a bone scan"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"A patient treated for thyroid cancer. A patient treated for thyroid cancer, I-131, 5.5 gigabecquerels","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"A patient treated for thyroid cancer"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"An industrial thickness gauge. An industrial thickness gauge, Cs-137, 37 gigabecquerels","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(167, 139, 250); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"An industrial thickness gauge"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"A sterilisation source. A sterilisation source, Co-60, 37 gigabecquerels","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"A sterilisation source"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-1","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Cs-137, 37 GBq — initially 0.077 mSv/h at 1 metre per GBq, worked out from its decay scheme. Physical half-life: 30.1 years."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"pt-dist","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Your distance"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","id":"pt-dist","type":"range","min":"0.3","max":"10","step":"0.1","aria-valuetext":"1 m","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"1"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"pt-dist","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"1 m"]],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mt-2 mb-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"Air. Shield with Air","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(148, 163, 184); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Air"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Water. Shield with Water","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Water"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Concrete. Shield with Concrete","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Concrete"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Steel. Shield with Steel","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Steel"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Lead. Shield with Lead","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Lead"]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"pt-thick","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Shield thickness"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"0","id":"pt-thick","type":"range","min":"0","max":"20","step":"0.5","aria-valuetext":"0 cm","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"0"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"pt-thick","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"0 cm"]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-chart-frame rounded-lg overflow-hidden border mt-2","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.35); height: 175px;"},["CANVAS",{"__playwright_bounding_rect__":"{\"left\":41,\"top\":81449.046875,\"right\":41,\"bottom\":81667.046875}","role":"img","data-a11y-static":"true","aria-describedby":"nk-protect-summary","aria-label":"Initial dose rate against distance for Cs-137 at 37 gigabecquerels. Unshielded it is 2.841 millisieverts per hour at 1 metre and 0.114 at 5 metres. At your chosen 1 metres behind 0 centimetres of air it is 2.841 millisieverts per hour.","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;"}]],["DIV",{"id":"nk-protect-summary","class":"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2 mt-2"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Initial dose rate"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(167, 139, 250);"},"2.84 mSv/h"]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(203, 213, 225, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Shield cuts it to"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"no shield"]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Dose in first hour"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"2.84 mSv"]]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"How long until you reach…"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"Public annual limit (1 mSv). Public annual limit, 1 millisieverts","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(56, 189, 248); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"Public annual limit (1 mSv)"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Worker annual limit (20 mSv). Worker annual limit, 20 millisieverts","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Worker annual limit (20 mSv)"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Radiation sickness begins (1000 mSv). Radiation sickness begins, 1000 millisieverts","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Radiation sickness begins (1000 mSv)"]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"21.1 minutes"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"to accumulate 1 mSv at 1 m, unshielded, after physical decay is included."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Sealed sources like this are safe because of the housing, not the isotope. Every serious accident with one has the same shape: the source came out of its shielding, or never went back in, and the person nearby had no way to know."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 font-bold","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"⏱️ With a steady source, halve your time and you halve your dose. A short-lived source changes while you wait, so this calculator integrates the falling rate."]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.376); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"⏱️ TIME"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Half target at 10.6 minutes"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Time is the free lever. This value includes radioactive decay instead of assuming the initial rate lasts forever."]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.376); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153);"},"📏 DISTANCE"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Move to 1.4 m"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"In the point-source, open-air model, multiply distance by 1.41 and the initial dose rate halves. Nearby extended sources and scattered radiation depart from this rule."]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2","style":"border-color: rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.376); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(96, 165, 250);"},"🧱 SHIELDING"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"+8,589.2 cm of air"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"In this narrow-beam model, one half-value layer halves the initial rate again. Scattered photons make real thick shields perform less neatly."]]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"For a source whose rate is effectively steady during a visit, the three halves multiply: 1/2 × 1/2 × 1/2 = 1/8 of the starting dose. The time card above uses decay-aware integration instead of forcing that shortcut onto short-lived medical isotopes."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Initial dose rate is computed from each nuclide's decay scheme with NIST mass energy-absorption coefficients for air, and time-to-dose integrates its physical half-life. The results sit within 3% of published gamma constants. The shield still uses the 1 MeV coefficients from section 5 and narrow-beam attenuation with no buildup factor, so a real thick shield performs somewhat worse. Patient geometry and biological clearance are also simplified. Treat this as the right order of magnitude and the right shape, never as a stay-time instruction."]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-accidents","data-nk-sec":"accidents","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-accidents","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.333) rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.333) rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.333) rgb(248, 113, 113); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-accidents","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.267);"},"📋 15. The three accidents, in the actual numbers"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"These are the events that shaped how the world thinks about nuclear power. The figures below come from UNSCEAR and the relevant national reports, and where the range is disputed the tool says so."],["DIV",{"class":"space-y-1"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Three Mile Island (1979)"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Pennsylvania, USA · INES 5"]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Chernobyl (1986)"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Ukraine, then USSR · INES 7"]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Fukushima Daiichi (2011)"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Japan · INES 7"]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"›"]]]]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"The evidence supports a narrower pattern: emergency responses can cause substantial non-radiological harm through evacuation, displacement, lost care and psychological distress. At Fukushima that harm is well documented; at Chernobyl its scale relative to projected radiation effects remains model-dependent. This is not an argument that radiation is harmless. It is why emergency planning has to weigh both kinds of harm."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Sources · reviewed 2026-08: ",["A",{"href":"https://www.unscear.org/unscear/en/publications/2020_2021_2.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"UNSCEAR Fukushima 2020/21"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.reconstruction.go.jp/files/user/topics/main-cat2/sub-cat2-6/20260213_kanrenshi.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"Japan Reconstruction Agency disaster-related deaths (2026)"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.mhlw.go.jp/english/topics/2011eq/workers/ri/ar/rat_12th.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"Japan MHLW Fukushima worker health report (2024)"]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-shelter","data-nk-sec":"shelter","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-shelter","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgb(163, 230, 53); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-shelter","style":"color: rgb(163, 230, 53); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.267);"},"🏠 16. Shelter or evacuate? Work the numbers"],["ASIDE",{"role":"note","aria-label":"Educational safety notice","class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.6); background: rgba(69, 10, 10, 0.35);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Educational model — not emergency or medical instructions"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(254, 202, 202);"},"In an actual release, follow state and local officials. Whether to shelter, evacuate, or take KI depends on measurements and conditions this model cannot know."],["A",{"href":"https://www.nrc.gov/about-nrc/emerg-preparedness/in-radiological-emerg","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"inline-block mt-1 text-[0.6875rem] font-bold underline","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"Official NRC emergency guidance ↗"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Fukushima Prefecture records 2,350 disaster-related deaths through 2025, a broad legal category that includes illness after injury and the physical burden of evacuation life. No acute radiation deaths occurred, and UNSCEAR has documented no resident health effects directly attributable to radiation. Worker compensation decisions are a separate category and do not prove individual causation. These figures cannot be reduced to a simple evacuation-versus-radiation score; they show why emergency choices have costs on both sides."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"In this deliberately limited dose model, sheltering combines two levers from section 14: a building is shielding, and staying put means less time in the open than driving through a plume. The arithmetic compares those dose paths only; medical vulnerability, changing plume direction and official measurements still govern a real decision."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"sh-rate","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Outdoor dose rate"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"2","id":"sh-rate","type":"range","min":"0.1","max":"30","step":"0.1","aria-valuetext":"2 mSv/h","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"2"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"sh-rate","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"2 mSv/h"]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"sh-plume","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Release lasts"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"8","id":"sh-plume","type":"range","min":"1","max":"72","step":"1","aria-valuetext":"8 h","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"8"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"sh-plume","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"8 h"]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"sh-evac","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Hours to get clear"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"4","id":"sh-evac","type":"range","min":"0.5","max":"12","step":"0.5","aria-valuetext":"4 h","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"4"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"sh-evac","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"4 h"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Where would you be sheltering?"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Outdoors, or in a car  ×0.9. Outdoors, or in a car, dose reduction factor 0.9","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Outdoors, or in a car  ×0.9"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Wood-frame house, ground floor  ×0.4. Wood-frame house, ground floor, dose reduction factor 0.4","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Wood-frame house, ground floor  ×0.4"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"true","aria-label":"Brick or concrete house  ×0.2. Brick or concrete house, dose reduction factor 0.2","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgb(251, 191, 36); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"Brick or concrete house  ×0.2"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Basement of a masonry house  ×0.05. Basement of a masonry house, dose reduction factor 0.05","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Basement of a masonry house  ×0.05"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Interior of a large concrete building  ×0.02. Interior of a large concrete building, dose reduction factor 0.02","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Interior of a large concrete building  ×0.02"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-1 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Mass is what matters, and masonry has several times the mass per square metre of a timber wall. Moving to an interior room, away from outside walls and windows, does more again."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Published range for this kind of building: ×0.1 – 0.3. The tool uses ×0.2."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-chart-frame rounded-lg overflow-hidden border mb-2","style":"border-color: rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.35); height: 180px;"},["CANVAS",{"__playwright_bounding_rect__":"{\"left\":41,\"top\":94430.359375,\"right\":41,\"bottom\":94648.359375}","role":"img","data-a11y-static":"true","aria-describedby":"nk-shelter-summary","aria-label":"Dose against how long it takes to get clear. Sheltering in a brick or concrete house through a 8 hour release gives a flat 3.2 millisieverts. Evacuating gives 7.2 millisieverts after 4 hours in the open. The two are equal at 1.8 hours: get clear faster than that and leaving costs less dose, slower and it costs more.","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;"}]],["DIV",{"id":"nk-shelter-summary","class":"grid grid-cols-2 gap-2"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Shelter here"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"3.2 mSv"]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg p-2 text-center","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.314);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Evacuate now"],["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"7.2 mSv"]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-sm font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(163, 230, 53);"},"On dose alone: stay where you are"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Break-even is 1.8 hours in the open. You said it would take 4 hours to get clear, which is longer than that, so the drive costs more dose than the walls save. This is the case people find counter-intuitive, and it is the ordinary one when a release is short and the roads are full."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Push the release out to several days and watch the answer flip: sheltering is a way of waiting out a plume, not a way of living somewhere contaminated. This classroom comparison cannot issue real guidance: officials may order sheltering or evacuation as measurements and travel conditions change."]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Sources · reviewed 2026-08: ",["A",{"href":"https://www.nrc.gov/about-nrc/emerg-preparedness/in-radiological-emerg","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"NRC radiological-emergency guidance"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.unscear.org/unscear/en/publications/2020_2021_2.html","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"UNSCEAR Fukushima 2020/21"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.reconstruction.go.jp/files/user/topics/main-cat2/sub-cat2-6/20260213_kanrenshi.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"Japan Reconstruction Agency disaster-related deaths (2026)"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.mhlw.go.jp/english/topics/2011eq/workers/ri/ar/rat_12th.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"Japan MHLW Fukushima worker health report (2024)"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mt-2 mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Where does that land against the published thresholds?"],["DIV",{"role":"list","class":"space-y-1"},["DIV",{"role":"listitem","class":"rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"US EPA protective action guide, lower bound — 10 mSv, first 4 days"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"At a projected 10 mSv, authorities are expected to act — evacuate or shelter, whichever gives the lower dose. Not \"evacuate\": whichever is lower."]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem","class":"rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"US EPA protective action guide, upper bound — 50 mSv, first 4 days"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"The top of the same range. Above this the case for moving people is strong enough that the disruption is usually judged worth it."]],["DIV",{"role":"listitem","class":"rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 border","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.06); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.2);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"IAEA generic criterion — 100 mSv, first 7 days"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"The international threshold for urgent protective action. Note it sits at the same 100 mSv as the lowest dose with a clearly measurable cancer link, from section 11."]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(248, 113, 113, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(248, 113, 113);"},"What this calculation leaves out, and it is the important part"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Everything above is dose, and radiation dose was not identified as the cause of deaths in Fukushima’s disaster-related-death total. Moving a hospital ward or a care home has risks that do not appear anywhere in this arithmetic: disrupted treatment, patients on ventilators, people with dementia moved somewhere unfamiliar, and prolonged displacement. Those stresses contributed to the official 2,350 total, but the legal category does not assign every case to one evacuation order. The lesson was not never evacuate; it was to decide per population rather than per map, because moving a frail patient can be more dangerous than moving a healthy adult."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mt-1.5 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"It also leaves out everything after the plume: contaminated ground, food and water controls, and whether people can return. A dose comparison over the first few days is one input to that decision, not the decision."]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Shielding factors from FEMA and EPA emergency planning guidance for cloud and ground shine, quoted as the ranges they are given as. Thresholds from the US EPA PAG Manual (2017) and IAEA GSR Part 7. The model is deliberately the simplest one that can flip: constant outdoor rate, a single building factor, and no credit for driving away from the plume rather than along it — which in a real evacuation matters as much as the hours do."]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-reactors","data-nk-sec":"reactors","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-reactors","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgb(56, 189, 248); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-reactors","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.267);"},"🏭 17. Reactor designs, and where SMRs really stand"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Every row says how it works, what makes it safe, and — the part usually left out — what the catch is."],["DIV",{"class":"space-y-1"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Pressurised water (PWR)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153); border: 1px solid rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.44);"},"operating"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"About 70% of the world fleet"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Boiling water (BWR)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153); border: 1px solid rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.44);"},"operating"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"About 15% of the fleet"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Heavy water (CANDU)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(52, 211, 153); border: 1px solid rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.44);"},"operating"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Canada, India, and others"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"RBMK (Chernobyl type)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225); border: 1px solid rgba(203, 213, 225, 0.44);"},"legacy"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"A handful still running in Russia"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Small modular (SMR)"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36); border: 1px solid rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.44);"},"emerging"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"A few operating; many proposed"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Molten salt"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(244, 114, 182); border: 1px solid rgba(244, 114, 182, 0.44);"},"proposed"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Prototypes only"]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold flex-1","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Fusion"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] font-black px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded-full","style":"color: rgb(244, 114, 182); border: 1px solid rgba(244, 114, 182, 0.44);"},"research"],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(56, 189, 248);"},"›"]],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] mt-0.5","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"No power on any grid"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.6);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(251, 191, 36);"},"On small modular reactors specifically"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"The engineering case is real: a small core can be cooled by convection and gravity alone, so a station blackout stops being the scenario that keeps operators awake. Factory production should also beat pouring concrete on site, where Western projects have overrun badly. But as of now almost none are operating commercially — China's HTR-PM since 2023, and a Russian floating plant. NuScale had the first US design approval and its flagship project was cancelled in 2023 when projected power costs rose from about $58 to $89 per MWh. Factory economics need order volume that does not yet exist, and several designs need HALEU fuel with a supply chain still being built. The right posture is interested, not convinced."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Sources · reviewed 2026-08: ",["A",{"href":"https://www.nuscalepower.com/press-releases/2023/utah-associated-municipal-power-systems-and-nuscale-power-agree-to-terminate-the-carbon-free-power-project","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"NuScale project termination"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://www.iter.org/node/20687/new-baseline-prioritize-robust-start-exploitation","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"ITER 2024 baseline"]," · ",["A",{"href":"https://annual.llnl.gov/fy-2022/national-ignition-facility-2022","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","class":"underline font-bold"},"LLNL NIF 2022 result"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-waste","data-nk-sec":"waste","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-waste","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.333) rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.333) rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.333) rgb(148, 163, 184); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-waste","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(203, 213, 225, 0.267);"},"🗄️ 18. The waste question, taken seriously"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"This is the objection that survives every other answer, so it deserves a straight one — including the part that genuinely has no solution."],["DIV",{"class":"space-y-1"},["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"How much there is"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"About 400,000 tonnes of spent fuel worldwide, growing by roughly 2,000–2,500 t a year."]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"How long it stays dangerous"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Radiotoxicity falls back to that of the original uranium ore after roughly 100,000 to 300,000 years."]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"Where it is right now"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Mostly on the sites that made it — first in cooling pools, then in dry casks."]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"The permanent answer"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Finland's Onkalo is the first deep geological repository in the world to be built and licensed."]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"›"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.07); border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22);"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 w-full text-left px-2.5 py-2 rounded-lg"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex items-center gap-2"},["SPAN",{"class":"flex-1"},["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","style":"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"},"The part nobody solved"],["SPAN",{"class":"block text-[0.6875rem]","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"How do you warn someone 10,000 years from now?"]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold","aria-hidden":"true","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"›"]]]]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-compare","data-nk-sec":"compare","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-compare","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.333) rgb(163, 230, 53); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-compare","style":"color: rgb(163, 230, 53); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.267);"},"⚖️ 19. Compared with the alternatives"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Risk only means something next to the risk of the thing you would do instead. Both charts are full life cycle, including mining, construction and accidents."],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg border p-2.5 mb-2","style":"border-color: rgba(163, 230, 53, 0.5); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-black mb-1","style":"color: rgb(163, 230, 53);"},"First, commit to an answer"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Answer these before you look. A chart you already agree with teaches you nothing; the gap between what you expected and what the data says is the part worth having."],["DIV",{"class":"mb-2"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Per unit of electricity, which has killed more people?"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Coal. Coal has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Coal"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Nuclear. Nuclear has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Nuclear"]]],["DIV",{"class":"mb-2"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"And which of these two?"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Hydropower. Hydropower has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Hydropower"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Nuclear. Nuclear has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Nuclear"]]],["DIV",{"class":"mb-2"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"One more — which of these?"],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Natural gas. Natural gas has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Natural gas"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Solar. Solar has caused more deaths per terawatt hour","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Solar"]]],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":"","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"background: transparent; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3); cursor: not-allowed;"},"Answer all three to compare (0 of 3)"]],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Deaths per terawatt-hour of electricity"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] rounded-lg border border-dashed p-2.5 leading-relaxed","style":"border-color: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.4); color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"The chart appears once you have answered the three questions above."],["P",{"class":"text-[0.625rem] mt-1","style":"color: rgb(148, 163, 184);"},"Logarithmic scale. Markandya & Wilkinson (2007) and Sovacool et al. (2016), compiled by Our World in Data. Nuclear's figure includes Chernobyl and Fukushima."],["DIV",{"class":"mt-2 rounded-lg border p-2.5","style":"border-color: rgba(132, 204, 22, 0.333); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.5);"},["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(163, 230, 53);"},"🤔 Nuclear power provokes far more fear than several sources that harm more people per unit of energy. What does that tell you about how people weigh a rare, dramatic, involuntary risk against a constant, invisible, familiar one?"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","class":"min-h-11 mt-1.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-black","style":"background: rgb(132, 204, 22); color: rgb(11, 16, 32); border: 1px solid rgb(132, 204, 22);"},"Worked it out? Check"]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-operate","data-nk-sec":"operate","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-operate","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.333) rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.333) rgba(52, 211, 153, 0.333) rgb(52, 211, 153); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba