ns left; each of the six beta steps moves one proton up and one neutron left, which is the zigzag. Radon-222, the only gas, sits in the middle at 86 protons and 136 neutrons.","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;","width":"560","height":"228"}]],[[1,148]],[[1,316]],[[1,322]],[[1,327]],[[1,332]]],[[1,406]],[[1,466]],[[1,517]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-binding","data-nk-sec":"binding","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-binding","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.333) rgb(56, 189, 248); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},[[1,519]],[[1,521]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-chart-frame rounded-lg overflow-hidden border mb-2","style":"border-color: rgba(56, 189, 248, 0.35); height: 190px;"},["CANVAS",{"__playwright_bounding_rect__":"{\"left\":41,\"top\":23076.78125,\"right\":41,\"bottom\":23294.78125}","role":"img","data-a11y-static":"true","aria-describedby":"nk-binding-description","aria-label":"Binding energy per nucleon against mass number. It climbs steeply from hydrogen at zero, through helium-4 at 7.07, peaks at nickel-62 at 8.795 MeV, then falls slowly to uranium-238 at 7.57. Light nuclei release energy by fusing up the left slope; heavy nuclei release it by splitting down the right slope.","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;","width":"560","height":"218"}]],[[1,525]],[[1,534]],[[1,540]],[[1,563]],[[1,565]],[[1,570]],[[1,575]]],[[1,678]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-biohalf","data-nk-sec":"biohalf","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-biohalf","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(244, 114, 182, 0.333) rgba(244, 114, 182