875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(196, 181, 253, 0.267);"},"⏳ 1. Half-life: stable under ordinary conditions"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"For a large sample, each half-life leaves half of what was there before — not half the original amount. Under ordinary laboratory and environmental conditions, temperature, pressure and chemistry do not measurably change most nuclear decay rates. Tiny exceptions exist for a few decay modes, especially electron capture, so “unchangeable” is an excellent practical rule rather than a universal law."],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap gap-1 mb-2"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Technetium-99m. Use Technetium-99m, half-life 6.0 hours","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Technetium-99m"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Radon-222. Use Radon-222, half-life 3.8 days","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Radon-222"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Iodine-131. Use Iodine-131, half-life 8.0 days","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","style":"background: rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.12); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.3);"},"Iodine-131"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-pressed":"false","aria-label":"Cobalt-60. Use Cobalt-60, half-life 5.3 years","data-nk-explored":"false","class":"min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-bold transition-colors","styl