e."],["DIV",{"class":"nk-slider flex items-center gap-2 mt-1.5"},["LABEL",{"for":"nk-c14","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-28 flex-shrink-0","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"C-14 remaining"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"50","id":"nk-c14","type":"range","min":"1","max":"100","step":"1","aria-valuetext":"50%","class":"nk-slider-input flex-1 min-w-0 min-h-11 accent-violet-500","value":"50"}],["OUTPUT",{"for":"nk-c14","class":"text-[0.6875rem] font-bold w-24 text-right","style":"color: rgb(196, 181, 253);"},"50%"]],["DIV",{"class":"flex flex-wrap items-end gap-2 mt-2"},["DIV",{"class":"flex-1 min-w-[150px]"},["LABEL",{"for":"nk-age-guess","class":"block text-[0.6875rem] font-bold mb-1","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Your estimate (years)"],["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"","id":"nk-age-guess","type":"number","placeholder":"e.g. 5730","class":"w-full min-h-11 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem]","value":"","style":"border: 1px solid rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.32); background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.8); color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"}]],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-label":"Reveal. Calculate the age of the sample","class":"min-h-11 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-[0.6875rem] font-black text-white","style":"background: rgb(14, 116, 144); border: 1px solid rgb(14, 116, 144);"},"Reveal"]]],["DIV",{"class":"nk-section-card rounded-xl border p-3 mt-4","id":"nksec-chain","data-nk-sec":"chain","aria-labelledby":"nkheading-chain","tabindex":"-1","style":"border-color: rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.333) rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.333) rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.333) rgb(192, 132, 252); border-left-width: 4px; border-left-style: solid; background-color: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.78); background-image: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.094) 0%, transparent 38%); box-shadow: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035) 0px 1px 0px inset, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85) 0px 16px 34px -26px; scroll-margin-top: 96px;"},["H4",{"class":"nk-section-heading font-black mb-3 pb-2","id":"nkheading-chain","style":"color: rgb(192, 132, 252); font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.35rem; letter-spacing: -0.01em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.267);"},"⛓️ 3. The chain from uranium to lead — and why radon is in basements"],["P",{"class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2","style":"color: rgb(203, 213, 225);"},"Most heavy nuclei do not reach stability in one step. Uranium-238 takes fourteen, alternating alpha and beta, and finishes as lead. One member of that chain is a gas, and that changes everything."],["DIV",{"class":"rounded-lg overflow-hidden border mb-2","style":"border-color: rgba(192, 132, 252, 0.35); height: 230px;"},["CANVAS",{"__playwright_bounding_rect__":"{\"left\":41,\"top\":6683.546875,\"right\":41,\"bottom\":6911.546875}","role":"img","data-a11y-static":"true","aria-describedby":"nk-chain-description","aria-label":"The uranium-238 chain plotted on the chart of nuclides, neutrons across and protons up. It starts at uranium-238 with 92 protons and 146 neutrons, top right, and walks down-left to lead-206 with 82 protons and 124 neutrons, bottom left. Each of the eight alpha steps moves two protons down and two neutrons left; each of the six beta steps moves one proton up and one neutron left, which is the zigzag. Radon-222, the only gas, sits in the middle at 86 protons and 136 neutrons.","width":"560","height":"228","style":"width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block;"}]],["P",{"id":"nk-chain-description","class":"text-[0.6875rem] mb-2 leading-relaxed","style":"color: rgb(226, 232, 240);"},"Every alpha step takes the same diagonal down-left; every beta step kicks back up-left at a shallower one. That sawtooth is not decoration — it is why the chain crosses the same elements more than once, and why uranium appears twice in the list below. Choose a row to light up its nucleus here."],["DIV",{"role":"list","aria-label":"Uranium-238 decay chain steps","class":"space-y-1 max-h-72 overflow-y-auto pr-1"},["DIV",{"role":"listitem"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button","aria-expanded":"false","c